    <string name="rules_title">📖 Hi-Lo System</string>
    <string name="rules_principle_title">🎯 The Principle</string>
    <string name="rules_principle_desc">The more high cards (10, J, Q, K, A) remain in the shoe, the more the player has the advantage. Hi-Lo allows you to track this mentally.</string>
    <string name="rules_values_title">🔢 The Values</string>
    <string name="rules_rc_title">📊 Running Count (RC)</string>
    <string name="rules_rc_desc">You add the values as the cards come out. Example: 5 (+1), K (−1), 3 (+1), 8 (0), 2 (+1) → RC = +2.</string>
    <string name="rules_tc_title">🎯 True Count (TC)</string>
    <string name="rules_tc_desc">In a casino, we play with several decks (often 6 or 8). The RC alone is not enough: it must be brought back to 1 deck.\n\nTC = RC / remaining decks\n\nExample: RC = +6, there are 3 decks left → TC = +2.\nIn general, TC ≥ +2 = player advantage, bet bigger.</string>
    <string name="rules_advice_title">💡 Training Advice</string>
    <string name="rules_advice_desc">Start slow (1500-2000 ms), small number of cards. When you are at 100% success, speed up. Pro goal: count a whole deck (52 cards) in less than 25 seconds.</string>
